# MASTER PROMPT: STAT-Psych India — Complete UI/UX Transformation for Emergency Psychiatric Clinical Decision Support

## ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior product designer, clinical UX specialist, mobile-first interface architect, and expert frontend engineer.

Continue working on the existing STAT-Psych India application. Improve its UI/UX directly in the current implementation.

STAT-Psych India is a clinical decision-support application intended to help clinicians navigate psychiatric emergencies in Indian emergency departments, psychiatric casualty units, and acute-care settings.

The application already contains clinical pathways, medication recommendations, dosing information, safety warnings, bedside assessments, patient-context modifiers, evidence references, triage tools, and clinical handover functionality.

The primary problem is not a lack of information. It is the way the information is presented.

The current experience is too dense, visually flat, text-heavy, and difficult to scan quickly. Important clinical actions compete with detailed rationale, study statistics, references, and supporting explanations. On mobile, this makes it unnecessarily difficult to identify the information that matters most.

Your task is to transform the application into a polished, modern, clinically focused, highly readable emergency decision-support interface.

**Implement the improvements directly in the existing application. Do not merely describe them, produce a mockup, or provide isolated code snippets.**

Preserve the current architecture where practical, all existing clinical functionality, and all source clinical content.

Do not rebuild the application from scratch unless a specific architectural limitation makes a targeted refactor necessary.

