Do not clear state simply because an accordion opens or a component changes.

Ensure that state does not leak incorrectly between unrelated clinical pathways.

Avoid flicker, unnecessary layout shifts, and unexpected scrolling.

## Safe rendering

Review the use of dynamic HTML rendering.

Use safe DOM APIs, appropriate escaping, and safe rendering patterns for clinical content, labels, and reference metadata.

Do not allow untrusted text or URLs to introduce HTML injection or script execution risks.

Validate external link destinations appropriately.

Keep the implementation maintainable and easy to extend when new pathways are added.

## Preserve existing functionality

Do not break:

- Syndrome selection.
- Tier selection.
- Stabilization checklist.
- Patient-context modifiers.
